- Until symptoms subside (not to exceed 3000mg in 24 hours)\n\nInstructions:\n- Take the medication with a full glass of water.\n- Do not take more than the recommended dose.\n- Rest and stay hydrated.\n- Isolate yourself to prevent transmission to others until fever has resolved for at least 24 hours without the use of fever-reducing medications.\n\nPrecautions:\n- Monitor your temperature daily.\n- Seek immediate medical attention if severe symptoms develop (e.g., difficulty breathing, chest pain, severe weakness).\n- Follow-up in 3-5 days if symptoms persist or worsen.\n- Practice good hand hygiene and respiratory etiquette to prevent transmission.\n- Be aware of the potential for dehydration due to fever and progression of viral infection leading to more severe illness (e.g., pneumonia).\n- Be mindful of the risk of transmission to others, particularly those who are vulnerable (e.g., elderly, immunocompromised).',992,992,'2025-10-09 22:22:37','2025-10-09 22:28:19',98),(46,54,'44','fever','Patient Information:\nName: Rizvi Mahmud Plabon\nAge: 33\nGender: Male\nMedical History: Not clearly provided\n\nCurrent Symptoms:\nFever\n\n1. Potential Differential Diagnoses:\n   - Viral infection (e.g., influenza, common cold)\n   - Bacterial infection (e.g., strep throat, urinary tract infection)\n   - COVID-19\n   - Malaria\n   - Other infectious diseases (e.g., tuberculosis, HIV)\n   - Autoimmune diseases (e.g., lupus, rheumatoid arthritis)\n   - Malignancies (e.g., lymphoma, leukemia)\n\n2. Recommended Diagnostic Tests:\n   - Complete Blood Count (CBC)\n   - Blood cultures\n   - Urinalysis\n   - Chest X-ray\n   - COVID-19 PCR test\n   - Malaria test\n   - If indicated, further specific tests for autoimmune diseases or malignancies\n\n3. Urgency Level: \n   - Medium: Fever is a common symptom but can indicate a serious condition if it persists or is accompanied by other severe symptoms.\n\n4. Key Observations and Clinical Notes:\n   - The patient\'s medical history is un